# apps/api/.dockerignore
#
# Keep the build context for apps/api/Dockerfile small and free of
# anything that should not be COPYed into the build stage. The
# final image is multi-stage so most of these never reach the
# runtime layer, but excluding them at the build-context level
# keeps the `docker build` cache line stable across code-only
# changes (e.g. swapping a test fixture should not invalidate
# the `go mod download` layer).

# Generated code that the test suite regenerates on demand -
# building a production binary never needs it. ent/ is kept
# because the production wiring imports generated packages from
# it; openapi/ is excluded because the production binary does
# not embed the spec.
openapi/

# Migration down-files are deliberately not executable by Atlas
# and are not needed for a build of the Go binary. The forward
# SQL files are similarly unused by `go build`.
migrations/*.down.sql.example
migrations/README.md

# Local-only / test-only files. None of these are imported by
# the production binary, but COPYing them inflates the build
# context and (more importantly) the on-disk builder stage.
**/*_test.go
**/testdata/
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Editor / OS noise. Not expected in this repo, but harmless to
# keep ignoring in case a developer machine adds them locally.
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
